#N canvas 40 40 1000 840 12;
#X text 20 20 u_level -- reports the level of a signal onto the disp bus. Tap it off anything you want to watch: it has no signal outlet and does not alter the audio., f 58;
#X text 20 95 creation arg 1: the name to report under \, e.g. in-l. REQUIRED -- without it the bus carries 0 as the name. inlets: one signal. outlets: none., f 58;
#X obj 20 220 inlet~;
#X obj 20 260 env~;
#X obj 20 350 f;
#X obj 20 380 i;
#X obj 20 410 change -1;
#X obj 20 440 list prepend \$1;
#X obj 20 470 list append dB;
#X obj 20 500 list trim;
#X obj 20 540 s disp;
#X obj 340 260 loadbang;
#X obj 340 290 del 200;
#X obj 340 320 metro 100;
#X text 340 360 Polled \, not pushed: env~ reports on its own window \, so its value is stored cold and banged at a fixed rate., f 46;
#X text 340 500 10 Hz is the sampling rate. Rate-limiting the draw is the display's job. C-5, f 46;
#X text 20 600 C-6, f 58;
#X text 20 700 env~ is RMS on a 0 to 100 dB scale (item 11 \, ref/module/audio.md). change -1: a steady signal stops reporting., f 58;
